00:53:59.960 --> 00:54:02.140
It's like the Starbucks coffee on Game of Thrones.
就像《权力的游戏》里出现的星巴克咖啡杯一样。

1233
00:54:02.340 --> 00:54:02.740
Exactly.
没错。

1234
00:54:02.740 --> 00:54:06.060
We had a fan question from Jen H.
我们收到了一位来自纽约的粉丝珍·H的提问。

1235
00:54:06.300 --> 00:54:06.900
in New York.
在纽约。

1236
00:54:07.500 --> 00:54:11.360
Jen says, I have a justice for Pam comment.
珍说，我有一个关于“为帕姆讨回公道”的评论。

1237
00:54:11.720 --> 00:54:12.740
Justice for Pam?
为帕姆讨回公道？

1238
00:54:12.900 --> 00:54:13.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1239
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:17.800
Jen says, I've been waiting so long to ask this.
珍说，我等了很久才问这个问题。

1240
00:54:18.220 --> 00:54:20.740
Jim offers Daryl a job at his new company.
吉姆邀请达里尔去他的新公司工作。

1241
00:54:21.120 --> 00:54:23.900
Why on earth did he not ask Pam to join?
他为什么就没想过邀请帕姆加入呢？

1242
00:54:24.200 --> 00:54:27.480
Why couldn't she be the graphic designer at Athlead?
为什么她不能成为Athlead公司的平面设计师呢？

1243
00:54:28.360 --> 00:54:33.680
It's wild because both Ryan and Michael believed in her art talents more than her own husband.
这太疯狂了，因为瑞安和迈克尔对她艺术天赋的信任甚至超过了她自己的丈夫。

1244
00:54:34.060 --> 00:54:37.600
Ryan asked her to make a logo in Season 4, Episode 2.
瑞安在第四季第二集里让她设计过标志。

1245
00:54:37.800 --> 00:54:42.420
And then in Season 4, Episode 5, Michael asked her to make a logo for the local ad.
然后在第四季第五集里，迈克尔让她为当地广告设计标志。

1246
00:54:42.820 --> 00:54:49.080
I bet Pam would have been much more receptive to moving to Philly if her dream job was also waiting for her.
我敢说，如果费城那边也有适合她的梦想工作，帕姆会更愿意搬过去的。

1247
00:54:49.660 --> 00:54:51.040
Well, Jen, I hear you.
好吧，珍，我听到你的心声了。

1248
00:54:51.220 --> 00:54:52.860
But I do have some thoughts.
但我确实有一些想法。

1249
00:54:53.160 --> 00:54:54.600
I have some thoughts as well.
我也有一些想法。

1250
00:54:54.600 --> 00:54:59.640
Well, first of all, Jim's business is not really making any money for this family.
首先，吉姆的生意并没有真正为这个家庭赚到什么钱。

1251
00:54:59.640 --> 00:55:09.200
And I had read another fan comment that said they were really ticked off at Pam because she's not supporting Jim's, like, dream job.
我还读到另一条粉丝评论，说他们真的很生帕姆的气，因为她不支持吉姆所谓的梦想工作。

1252
00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:12.360
Like, why didn't she just get a job in Philly?
比如，她为什么不直接去费城找份工作呢？

1253
00:55:12.760 --> 00:55:15.580
Her husband's making so much money at this great job.
她丈夫在这份很棒的工作上赚了很多钱。

1254
00:55:15.720 --> 00:55:17.340
But Jim is not making any money.
但吉姆根本没赚到钱。

1255
00:55:17.660 --> 00:55:18.220
Remember?
还记得吗？

1256
00:55:18.480 --> 00:55:20.980
It's like this company has not had a profit.
这家公司好像一直没盈利。

1257
00:55:21.200 --> 00:55:25.780
So if they're both working there, then no one's really bringing home a significant paycheck.
所以如果他们俩都在那儿工作，那家里其实没人能拿回像样的薪水。

1258
00:55:26.340 --> 00:55:30.220
Also, I don't think graphic design is Pam's dream job.
而且，我觉得平面设计也不是帕姆的梦想工作。

1259
00:55:30.400 --> 00:55:31.940
I don't think she—she didn't love it.
我觉得她……她并不喜欢。

1260
00:55:32.020 --> 00:55:33.440
She dropped out because she didn't love it.
她退学就是因为她不喜欢。

1261
00:55:33.520 --> 00:55:36.360
Yeah, she dropped out because it wasn't what she thought it was going to be.
没错，她退学是因为那跟她想象的不一样。

1262
00:55:36.680 --> 00:55:38.360
I would also say this.
我还要说一点。

1263
00:55:38.760 --> 00:55:41.840
If Jim and Pam are really hoping this business takes off,
如果吉姆和帕姆真的希望这项事业能成功，

1264
00:55:42.080 --> 00:55:53.980
they can't move to a whole new city with their children and invest in property or a big enough rental for all of them without knowing it's going to be a success.
在确定它会成功之前，他们不能带着孩子搬到一个全新的城市，去投资房产或者租一套足够大的房子。

1265
00:55:53.980 --> 00:55:59.960
Right now, you would assume they don't really have a house payment, and their kids are in school there.
目前来看，你可以认为他们没有房贷压力，而且孩子们也在那儿上学。

1266
00:56:00.420 --> 00:56:03.940
They have Pam's family, Jim's family nearby to help.
他们有帕姆的家人和吉姆的家人在附近帮忙。

1267
00:56:04.920 --> 00:56:11.080
So moving the whole family there, you're not going to do that until you know that this is really going to take off.
所以，在确定这事儿真的能成之前，你是不会把全家都搬过去的。

1268
00:56:11.340 --> 00:56:11.500
Yeah.
没错。

1269
00:56:12.040 --> 00:56:17.900
And I think there needs to be someone in this family who has, like, a stable income.
而且我觉得这个家里得有一个人有稳定的收入。

1270
00:56:17.900 --> 00:56:21.740
But, Jen, I appreciate you sticking up for Pam.
不过，简，我很感激你为帕姆说话。

1271
00:56:22.060 --> 00:56:24.380
Yes, Jen, I appreciate justice for Pam.
是的，简，我很感激你为帕姆主持公道。

1272
00:56:24.780 --> 00:56:29.960
I do see, like, down the road there might be a job opportunity there for sure.
我确实觉得，从长远来看，那儿肯定会有工作机会的。

1273
00:56:30.220 --> 00:56:30.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1274
00:56:31.420 --> 00:56:36.060
Aunt Shirley has had plenty of schnapps and has fallen asleep on the couch.
雪莉阿姨喝了太多杜松子酒，已经在沙发上睡着了。

1275
00:56:36.300 --> 00:56:38.740
Yeah, she hit the homemade schnapps really hard.
是啊，她自制的杜松子酒喝得太猛了。

1276
00:56:39.200 --> 00:56:45.380
Dwight says, okay, let's get her out in the yard and spray her down in a very tasteful, rustic, private shower.
德怀特说，好吧，我们把她弄到院子里，用一种非常有品位、质朴且私密的淋浴方式给她冲冲凉。

1277
00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:51.480
This is setting us up for the beginning of Moving On, Part 2, for which we got a lot of fan questions.
这为我们接下来要讲的《继续前行》第二部分做了铺垫，我们收到了很多粉丝关于这一集的提问。

1278
00:56:52.020 --> 00:56:53.520
We'll get to it next week.
我们下周再聊这个。

1279
00:56:54.380 --> 00:57:01.020
Meanwhile, Andy has called Pete into his office, and he tells Pete that he has contracted schlamydia.
与此同时，安迪把皮特叫进了办公室，告诉皮特他得了“施拉米迪亚”（schlamydia）。

1280
00:57:01.360 --> 00:57:01.880
Yeah.
没错。

1281
00:57:02.180 --> 00:57:02.920
From Aaron.
从亚伦那儿传染的。

1282
00:57:03.360 --> 00:57:03.620
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1283
00:57:03.840 --> 00:57:08.120
He's trying to get Pete's reaction, and we talked about this with Jake Lacey.
他想看看皮特的反应，我们和杰克·莱西聊过这个。

1284
00:57:08.660 --> 00:57:09.380
We did.
我们聊过。

1285
00:57:09.380 --> 00:57:13.060
He said that schlamydia was an improv by Ed.
他说“施拉米迪亚”是艾德即兴发挥的。

1286
00:57:13.060 --> 00:57:17.060
It was, because in the script it said, Aaron gave me incurable syphilis.
确实是，因为剧本里写的是：亚伦传染给了我无法治愈的梅毒。

1287
00:57:18.000 --> 00:57:18.880
Pretty lame, huh?
挺烂的，对吧？

1288
00:57:19.180 --> 00:57:22.260
But then Ed improvised schlamydia.
但后来艾德即兴改成了“施拉米迪亚”。

1289
00:57:22.660 --> 00:57:25.560
He did, and it made Jake laugh.
他改了，而且把杰克逗笑了。

1290
00:57:25.900 --> 00:57:27.100
I found the blooper.
我找到了这段花絮。

1291
00:57:27.300 --> 00:57:28.060
Let's hear it.
我们来听听看。

1292
00:57:28.740 --> 00:57:37.300
I just got a phone with my doctor, and it turns out that I contracted schlamydia.
我刚和医生通完电话，结果发现我得了施拉米迪亚。

1293
00:57:37.300 --> 00:57:37.400
Schlamydia.
施拉米迪亚。

1294
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:41.880
Come on.
得了吧。

1295
00:57:42.380 --> 00:57:43.340
Come on.
得了吧。

1296
00:57:44.580 --> 00:57:45.060
Schlamydia.
施拉米迪亚。

1297
00:57:47.540 --> 00:57:48.320
Oh, man.
天哪。

1298
00:57:48.620 --> 00:57:52.620
Well, I guess they loved it so much they kept it in, and then they had to do it again and
好吧，我想他们太喜欢这个梗了，所以保留了下来，然后他们不得不一遍又一遍地重拍，

1299
00:57:52.620 --> 00:57:54.240
again so that Jake didn't laugh.
直到杰克不再笑场为止。

1300
00:57:54.720 --> 00:57:55.120
Yes.
是的。

1301
00:57:55.280 --> 00:58:00.160
And Jake told us that his proudest performance moment on the whole show was in this scene
杰克告诉我们，他在整部剧中感到最自豪的表演时刻就是这一场戏，

1302
00:58:01.360 --> 00:58:06.540
because there's that long pause, and Pete says, you were gone.
因为中间有那段长长的停顿，然后皮特说，你当时不在。

1303
00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:09.340
And Jake improvised that.
那是杰克即兴发挥的。

1304
00:58:09.480 --> 00:58:14.460
And then in the moment, Ed as Andy reacted and improvised, I knew it.
在那一刻，饰演安迪的艾德也即兴做出了反应，说我知道了。

1305
00:58:14.640 --> 00:58:16.880
And Jake just said it was the coolest thing.
杰克说那是整场戏最酷的部分。

1306
00:58:17.120 --> 00:58:17.380
Yeah.
没错。

1307
00:58:17.520 --> 00:58:22.080
And then what's really cool is after that little moment of improv from both of them,
真正酷的是，在他们两人那段小小的即兴表演之后，

1308
00:58:22.180 --> 00:58:23.500
they get back on script.
他们又回到了剧本的轨道上。

1309
00:58:23.660 --> 00:58:23.940
Yes.
是的。

1310
00:58:24.220 --> 00:58:26.760
And finish the scene, which is, oh, just delicious.
并完成了那场戏，真是太精彩了。

1311
00:58:27.420 --> 00:58:32.220
The line that got them back on script was Pete saying, and just so you know, there was
让他们回到剧本的那句台词是皮特说的，而且你要知道，并没有

1312
00:58:32.220 --> 00:58:33.080
no overlap.
重叠。

1313
00:58:33.360 --> 00:58:35.320
And then they were back as scripted.
然后他们就回到了剧本设定的内容。

1314
00:58:35.320 --> 00:58:42.860
However, this does end with another improv when Andy starts to sing the song, Bad Day.
不过，这场戏最后又出现了一段即兴表演，当时安迪开始唱《倒霉的一天》这首歌。

1315
00:58:43.120 --> 00:58:44.440
We had a bad day.
我们倒霉的一天。

1316
00:58:44.820 --> 00:58:45.040
Different lyrics.
歌词改了。

1317
00:58:45.480 --> 00:58:46.340
What did it do?
那是怎么回事？

1318
00:58:46.660 --> 00:58:47.120
Yes.
是的。

1319
00:58:47.440 --> 00:58:51.200
From Steve Burgess, he said we had to get permission to change the lyrics.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，我们必须获得许可才能更改歌词。

1320
00:58:51.360 --> 00:58:54.780
They were okay with using different lyrics, and it cost $20,000.
他们同意使用不同的歌词，但这花了2万美元。

1321
00:58:55.420 --> 00:58:58.600
And he said, by the way, this wasn't scripted.
他说，顺便提一下，这并不是剧本里写的。

1322
00:58:58.700 --> 00:59:02.240
So after Ed did it in the scene, they had to make sure they could get it cleared.
所以艾德在戏里演完之后，他们必须确保能获得授权。

1323
00:59:02.440 --> 00:59:03.060
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1324
00:59:03.520 --> 00:59:08.040
After this scene, we see Andy and Toby, and Toby's like, hey, you cannot fire Pete.
这场戏之后，我们看到了安迪和托比，托比说，嘿，你不能解雇皮特。

1325
00:59:08.420 --> 00:59:10.980
You can't fire someone just because you have a grudge.
你不能仅仅因为有私怨就解雇别人。

1326
00:59:11.220 --> 00:59:12.920
The same thing happened with Nellie.
内莉那次也是一样。

1327
00:59:13.080 --> 00:59:14.300
And Andy's like, no, no, no.
安迪说，不，不，不。

1328
00:59:14.600 --> 00:59:16.320
That was a professional grudge.
那是公事上的积怨。

1329
00:59:16.420 --> 00:59:17.740
This is a personal grudge.
这是私怨。

1330
00:59:17.900 --> 00:59:18.220
Yes.
没错。

1331
00:59:18.640 --> 00:59:22.720
And then Toby shows Andy that Aaron and Pete have disclosed their relationship.
然后托比向安迪展示了艾琳和皮特已经申报了他们的关系。

1332
00:59:23.020 --> 00:59:25.060
You know, they fill out that form in Human Resources.
你知道，他们填了人力资源部的那张表格。

1333
00:59:26.280 --> 00:59:28.480
Andy is furious and crumples it up.
安迪非常愤怒，把它揉成了一团。

1334
00:59:29.040 --> 00:59:31.120
Toby's like, that's not the original.
托比说，那不是原件。

1335
00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:32.760
So, you know, it's not a big deal.
所以，你知道，这没什么大不了的。

1336
00:59:33.040 --> 00:59:34.620
I just love that one detail.
我特别喜欢这个细节。

1337
00:59:34.800 --> 00:59:38.760
And then as Andy walks away, Toby uncrumples it and is like, it is the original.
然后当安迪走开时，托比把它展平，说，这就是原件。

1338
00:59:39.100 --> 00:59:40.880
Well, I looked this up in the script.
嗯，我查了一下剧本。

1339
00:59:41.460 --> 00:59:48.380
As scripted, Andy was supposed to fold up the document and put it in his pocket and then kick Toby's chair and walk out.
按照剧本，安迪本应把文件折好放进口袋，然后踢一下托比的椅子走出去。

1340
00:59:48.380 --> 00:59:55.700
And Toby's last line was, it's not the original, but instead, Ed crumpled it up and threw it at him.
托比的最后一句台词是，那不是原件，但艾德把它揉成一团扔向了他。

1341
00:59:55.840 --> 00:59:59.800
And he was like, it's not the original and kicked the trash can.
他说，那不是原件，然后踢了垃圾桶。

1342
01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:02.620
And so Paul improvised.
所以保罗即兴发挥了。

1343
01:00:03.320 --> 01:00:04.200
Uncrumpling it.
把它展平。

1344
01:00:04.380 --> 01:00:06.640
Uncrumpling it and saying, it was the original.
把它展平并说，这就是原件。

1345
01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:07.780
That is great.
那太棒了。

1346
01:00:07.980 --> 01:00:09.220
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

1347
01:00:09.440 --> 01:00:10.540
So fun.
太有趣了。

1348
01:00:10.880 --> 01:00:11.520
All right.
好了。

1349
01:00:11.520 --> 01:00:13.860
Are you ready for Pam to get to her interview?
你准备好去看帕姆的面试了吗？

1350
01:00:14.400 --> 01:00:16.980
I am per the call sheets.
根据通告单，我已经准备好了。

1351
01:00:16.980 --> 01:00:20.640
This was the very first scene of this entire episode that was filmed.
这是整集中拍摄的第一个场景。

1352
01:00:20.880 --> 01:00:21.060
Yep.
没错。

1353
01:00:21.240 --> 01:00:21.840
Monday morning.
周一早上。

1354
01:00:22.000 --> 01:00:24.820
Monday morning, scene 24, first up on Monday.
周一早上，第24场，周一的第一场戏。

1355
01:00:24.960 --> 01:00:26.740
It was described like this.
剧本是这样描述的。

1356
01:00:26.900 --> 01:00:31.780
Interior real estate company, Pam meets the Michael Scott of real estate, Mark.
内景，房地产公司，帕姆遇到了房地产界的迈克尔·斯科特，马克。

1357
01:00:32.240 --> 01:00:35.420
And I saw on the call sheet that you and Bob had 6 a.m.
我在通告单上看到你和鲍勃是早上6点

1358
01:00:35.520 --> 01:00:37.740
call times, but the rest of us got to come in at 1.
开工，但我们其他人是下午1点才到。

1359
01:00:38.020 --> 01:00:38.300
Yep.
没错。

1360
01:00:38.760 --> 01:00:40.400
This was a location.
这是一个外景地。

1361
01:00:40.400 --> 01:00:42.440
We did not build these offices.
这些办公室不是我们搭建的。

1362
01:00:42.440 --> 01:00:44.000
And I remembered that very clearly.
我对此记得非常清楚。

1363
01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:51.180
We got ready on set, and then we drove to this location in a series of vans.
我们在片场准备好后，就坐着几辆面包车来到了这个外景地。

1364
01:00:51.300 --> 01:00:54.840
So Bob and I got to share a van ride over to the set.
所以我和鲍勃共乘一辆车去了片场。

1365
01:00:55.080 --> 01:00:58.660
Listen, any time I got to share with Bob, I was just so tickled.
听着，任何能和鲍勃共处的时光，我都感到非常开心。

1366
01:00:58.800 --> 01:00:59.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1367
01:00:59.020 --> 01:01:00.780
So I remember that car ride.
所以我记得那次车程。

1368
01:01:00.920 --> 01:01:05.120
We got a lot of fan questions about what it was like for me to get to work with Bob.
我们收到了很多粉丝提问，问我能和鲍勃合作是什么感觉。

1369
01:01:05.420 --> 01:01:06.400
One from Natalie L.
其中一位来自马里兰州巴尔的摩的娜塔莉·L.

1370
01:01:06.520 --> 01:01:10.560
in Baltimore, Maryland, who just said, what was it like working with Bob Odenkirk?
她问，和鲍勃·奥登科克合作是什么感觉？

1371
01:01:10.560 --> 01:01:12.780
I laughed all morning.
我那天早上笑个不停。

1372
01:01:13.100 --> 01:01:15.540
I only had him from 6 a.m.
我只和他从早上6点

1373
01:01:15.680 --> 01:01:17.560
to 1 p.m., but oh, my goodness.
待到下午1点，但天哪，真是太棒了。

1374
01:01:17.860 --> 01:01:22.900
And one of my favorite moments that I couldn't get over and that I still can't get over when I watch it,
我最喜欢的时刻之一，让我难以忘怀，即使现在看回放也依然觉得好笑，

